@startuml
title Order Lifecycle - 8 States / 8 Business Transitions\nBR15 / BR16 / BR17 | UC01 and HT03
footer Team 524H0072 / 524H0189 / 524H0188 | UC01 review: Nguyen Hai Trieu | AI-assisted draft
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFCF5
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #FFF4DF
skinparam stateBorderColor #735344
skinparam ArrowColor #735344
hide empty description
state Placed
state Confirmed
state Preparing
state Ready
state "Out for Delivery" as Out
state Delivered #E6F0E1
state Cancelled #FCE8E2
state Failed #FCE8E2
[*] --> Placed : successful placement
Placed --> Confirmed : Kitchen Staff\n[own hub]
Placed --> Cancelled : Customer [own order]\nor Kitchen Staff [own hub; reason required]
Confirmed --> Preparing : Kitchen Staff\n[own hub]
Confirmed --> Cancelled : Customer [own order]\nor Admin
Preparing --> Ready : Kitchen Staff\n[own hub]
Ready --> Out : Shipper\n[assigned to this order]
Out --> Delivered : assigned Shipper\n[online-paid OR COD cash confirmed]
Out --> Failed : assigned Shipper\n[customer unreachable]
Delivered --> [*]
Cancelled --> [*]
Failed --> [*]
note right of Placed
  Edit items only in Placed (BR17).
  Reuse original time/load/rain.
  Edit does not change the Order state.
end note
note right of Ready
  Assignment policy is AMB01:
  proposed manual Admin assignment at Ready;
  not an extra Order state or transition.
end note
note left of Cancelled
  FULL simulated refund if paid online (BR16).
  Retain order, lines and history.
end note
note right of Failed
  Financial policy after Failed is AMB02;
  BR16 cancellation refund is a separate rule.
end note
legend bottom
  Check every action in the business layer, including actor scope.
  Delivered, Cancelled and Failed have no outgoing business transitions.
  Reject every unlisted transition; UI visibility alone is insufficient.
  Initial/final arrows are not the eight business transitions.
endlegend
@enduml
